**Context:** All test addresses start with 10 native coin (ETH/BNB/… by chain). Do not send more native coin per call than this budget allows. Use at most 12 calls per sequence.

**Goal:** Scale ETH amounts on payable calls to probe value-sensitive code paths and unlock underpriced attack angles.

**Technique:**
Choose one payable call in the seed and multiply its ETH value by a factor:
  0× (set to 0 wei), 0.1×, 0.5×, 1.5×, 2×, or 10×.
- If value is already 0 on a payable call, treat 1 ETH ("0xde0b6b3a7640000") as the baseline before scaling.
- If the seed has a very large value, also try reducing it — some checks trigger only below a threshold.
- Produce variants at multiple scales so coverage spans the value-sensitive range.

**Value hints:** Use "0x0", "0xde0b6b3a7640000" (1 ETH), "0x1bc16d674ec80000" (2 ETH), "0x8ac7230489e80000" (10 ETH), "0x3635c9adc5dea00000" (1000 ETH).

